From: Win7 port restore
Subject: [PATCH] desktop/ActivitySettings: stop the profile title from truncating before the column is full

The Activity profile header renders the display name in a
shrink-to-fit centred flex row (justify-center gap-2) and gives the
<h1> a self-referential max-width:

  max-w-[min(720px,calc(100%-2.25rem))]

The 100% resolves against that same row, and 2.25rem is the 36px the
sibling edit button (gap-2 8px + h-7/w-7 28px) occupies, so the
heading's own width feeds back into its cap: h1 <= min(text, row - 36)
<= row - 36. Whenever the row is narrower than roughly the text plus
36px the heading is clamped and truncate adds the ellipsis, even
though the surrounding column has room — the two subtitle lines on the
same page carry only max-w-full, render fully, and are wider than the
heading, which is what pinpoints the clamp as the cause rather than the
column. In the shipped 800px window "cc-haha" came out as "cc-ha…";
maximised the row crosses the threshold and it renders in full.

Take the edit button out of the row's flow instead of reserving room
for it: the button becomes absolute (inset-y-0 right-0 my-auto, so it
centres against the title line without touching active:translate-y) and
the row grows to w-full, which makes the heading's cap a plain fixed
max-w-[720px]. The heading can now use the full content column and the
ellipsis only appears once the text genuinely reaches 720px. The button
keeps its group/activity-profile parent, opacity-0 default and
group-hover/focus-visible reveal, so the existing assertions in
ActivitySettings.test.tsx still hold unchanged.

A regression test locks the fix in: the <h1> must carry the plain
max-w-[720px] and no calc(100%-2.25rem), and the edit control must be
absolute/inset-y-0/right-0 without the old shrink-0 in-flow sizing.

diff --git a/desktop/src/pages/ActivitySettings.test.tsx b/desktop/src/pages/ActivitySettings.test.tsx
index 22c187c84..ced3a4563 100644
--- a/desktop/src/pages/ActivitySettings.test.tsx
+++ b/desktop/src/pages/ActivitySettings.test.tsx
@@ -285,6 +285,23 @@ describe('ActivitySettings', () => {
     expect(editButton.closest('div')).toHaveClass('group/activity-profile')
   })
 
+  it('lets the profile title span the full column instead of reserving room for the edit control', async () => {
+    render(<ActivitySettings />)
+
+    await flushActivityLoad()
+
+    const title = screen.getByRole('heading', { level: 1 })
+    expect(title).toHaveClass('max-w-[720px]')
+    expect(title.className).not.toContain('calc(100%-2.25rem)')
+
+    const editButton = screen.getByRole('button', { name: 'Edit profile' })
+    expect(editButton).toHaveClass('absolute')
+    expect(editButton).toHaveClass('inset-y-0')
+    expect(editButton).toHaveClass('right-0')
+    expect(editButton).not.toHaveClass('shrink-0')
+    expect(editButton.closest('div')).toHaveClass('relative')
+  })
+
   it('uses a compact summary strip instead of the loose card layout', async () => {
     render(<ActivitySettings />)
 
